she studied the walls and the door with its curtain. The building had only\line one room, and this one was smaller than the other where the family\line huddled. We were only a twice-handful: three males, three females, one\line 
neuter and three children... the travel had not been kind to us. And why\line do the Jokka roam? "Because the Jokka have always roamed." So Darisil\line said.\line \~ \~ \~ \~Into the sepia shadows went Kediil, to sit by Sedikit's bedside\line 
and touch him without any visible fear. She peeled back his lips to\line examine his gums, stared into his eyes, brushed his forehead, his nose,\line his sides. "How long has he been sick? Has he eaten? Has he passed waste?\line 
Has he vomited? How is his speech when he speaks?" And on and on the\line questions went. I answered as well as I could. When she'd learned all she\line deemed necessary, she stood and stretched.\line \~ \~ \~ \~
