know that staying in one place will bring its own hardships?"\line \~ \~ \~ \~"Of course," I said. "But a new danger may be an easier one." I\line smiled. "We make of life what we can."\line \~ \~ \~ \~
Kediil searched my eyes--an unmistakable examination, her own gaze\line unblinking and bright. Her eyes had a beautiful color, a green-blue that\line suggested deep water. She withdrew her hands and took a deep breath. The\line 
packets she handed to me were fragrant with the scent of life.\line \~ \~ \~ \~"I would like to have stayed and mixed these properly, but they\line will do some good as long as they're ground. They should help."\line \~ \~ \~ \~
